course: dictionary
lesson: 2862
title: Dome
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dome is a round roof shaped like half of a ball. The words around it give you clues: «The Romans used arches, domes and concrete» tells you a dome is a kind of building shape. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: The word can also mean anything shaped like half a ball. «The dome of the sky» is not a roof, but the sky looks rounded over us, like half a ball. «A glass dome» and «a snow dome» work the same way: they are rounded tops that cover something.
explain: Look for the clue words round, half and shape. When you read about a planetarium, «a dome-shaped room that shows the night sky on its ceiling» tells you the shape straight away: the room's ceiling is curved like half a ball.
fact: A dome is a noun. One is a dome, and more than one is domes.
fact: A dome is a round roof shaped like half of a ball.
fact: In science and maths, a dome is a half-sphere, a strong shape that spreads weight evenly.
fact: «The Pantheon in Rome, nearly 1,900 years old, still has the world's largest unreinforced concrete dome.»
fact: «Pachycephalosaurus had a bony dome up to 25 centimetres thick.» Here a dome means the rounded top of a head.
exercise: «The Romans used arches, domes and concrete.» What is a dome? | * A round roof shaped like half of a ball | A kind of loaf of bread | A long, flat road | A small pond with fish in it
exercise: «A planetarium is a dome-shaped room that shows the night sky on its ceiling.» What does dome-shaped mean? | * Shaped like half a ball | Shaped like a square box | Flat, like a sheet of paper | Shaped like a long, thin snake
exercise: «Pachycephalosaurus had a bony dome up to 25 centimetres thick.» What does dome mean here? | Hair that is curly | A type of cave | * The rounded, thick top of a head | A hard, flat road
test: «A snow dome sat on the shelf, with tiny houses inside.» What is a snow dome? | A kind of cloud that falls as rain | A box for storing shoes | * A rounded glass cover with snow inside | A tall, thin tower
test: Which word is the plural of dome? | domer | * domes | dome's | domen
exam: «Dung beetles ... went straight even under a starry sky in a planetarium, a dome-shaped room that shows the night sky on its ceiling.» In this sentence, what is a dome-shaped room? | * A room shaped like half a ball, showing the night sky on its ceiling | A room with square walls and a flat roof | A dark cellar under the ground | A room with a curved ceiling shaped like half a ball, showing the night sky
